# MadGraph5 batch script: p p > j j on MadGraph's shipped run-card defaults.
#
# Why this exact process:
#   - The canonical leading-order QCD process, and the only one in the set whose
#     flavour group mixes subprocesses with *unequal* identical-particle
#     symmetry factors: g g > g g and q q~ > g g carry 1/2, q g > q g and
#     g g > q q~ carry 1. A group-wide factor taken from one member is wrong for
#     the others here, where in every other multi-channel row it happens to be
#     right.
#   - Its scale is the general case rather than a degenerate one: a 2 -> 2 core
#     of massless coloured legs at dynamical_scale_choice = -1, where the
#     clustering has real freedom in which pair it merges and no closed form
#     collapses the prescription.
#
# The run card is left at the shipped defaults — dynamical scale, ptj 20,
# etaj 5, 10000 events, use_syst on — with two departures:
#
#   - ebeam1 = ebeam2 = 6500, stated rather than inherited, which is the value
#     the defaults already carry and the energy every other hadronic reference
#     here runs at.
#   - pdlabel = lhapdf with lhaid 247000 (NNPDF23_lo_as_0130_qed) in place of
#     the MG-internal nn23lo1. nn23lo1 is not an LHAPDF6 grid and cannot be read
#     by this crate's PDF layer, so a run taking it could not be compared
#     against at all; 247000 is the set the Drell-Yan, llj and b b~ references
#     already use.
#
# The default jet cuts are the whole regulator: uncut, the cross section is
# dominated by the collinear and soft region, so ptj 20 is what makes the
# comparison measure the matrix element and the scale rather than the cutoff.
generate p p > j j
output pp_to_jj -nojpeg
launch
  set ebeam1 6500
  set ebeam2 6500
  set pdlabel lhapdf
  set lhaid 247000
  done
